// Jenkinsfile.survey — drop-in stage for the dagtools per-build survey.
//
// Add this to your repo's Jenkinsfile alongside its existing build / test
// stages. Once a repo joins the qualification system the dagster-survey
// stage is mandatory; it gates on the repo's Definitions actually loading,
// then publishes a structural inventory to the MinIO registry under
// inventory/<repo>/<sha>/.
//
// Environment expectations (set globally or in a shared Jenkins library):
//   DAGTOOLS_REGISTRY     e.g. "s3://dag-tools"
//   DAGTOOLS_S3_ENDPOINT  e.g. "https://minio.internal:9000"
//   AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID, AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY   (or instance role)
//   REPO_NAME             friendly repo identifier — primary registry partition key
//   GIT_COMMIT, BUILD_ID  provided by Jenkins
//
// Recipe rule: a load failure fails the Jenkins stage and **nothing is
// published**. The registry never contains an inventory for code that
// doesn't load. ``dagtools survey`` exits 2 on load failure, which fails
// the stage automatically.
//
// The optional 'dagster-canary' stage (continuous early-warning for the
// next Dagster version) will land alongside the ``dagtools canary``
// subcommand in a follow-up commit; this template will be updated then.

stage('dagster-survey') {
  steps {
    sh '''
      python -m pip install --upgrade pip
      python -m pip install "dag_tools[qual]"
      dagtools \
        --registry "${DAGTOOLS_REGISTRY}" \
        --endpoint-url "${DAGTOOLS_S3_ENDPOINT}" \
        survey \
          --introspect \
          --locations workspace.yaml \
          --repo "${REPO_NAME}" \
          --sha "${GIT_COMMIT}" \
          --build "${BUILD_ID}"
    '''
  }
}
